WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.859 --> 00:00:03.968
- When I first started
climbing, I started going

00:00:03.968 --> 00:00:07.992
to all types of climbing
events, and I noticed

00:00:07.992 --> 00:00:10.952
I was the only person of color.

00:00:10.952 --> 00:00:13.613
I went home and I was
online, and I searched,

00:00:13.613 --> 00:00:15.395
do black people rock climb,
'cause I was really curious

00:00:15.395 --> 00:00:17.597
and my goal was to try and find

00:00:17.597 --> 00:00:20.008
where are all the black climbers?

00:00:20.008 --> 00:00:22.950
I found these forums that said,
"Black people don't climb,"

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:25.624
and I wanted to prove them wrong.

00:00:25.624 --> 00:00:29.868
(soft acoustic guitar music)

00:00:29.868 --> 00:00:32.127
Growing up, going into
the woods, going outdoors,

00:00:32.127 --> 00:00:34.297
it was something that
black people didn't do,

00:00:34.297 --> 00:00:35.614
you know, at least that's what I was told.

00:00:35.614 --> 00:00:37.241
In New York City, you didn't really have

00:00:37.241 --> 00:00:38.961
too many options for sports.

00:00:38.961 --> 00:00:42.303
It was either basketball,
football, or baseball

00:00:42.303 --> 00:00:44.263
if you were close enough to a park.

00:00:44.263 --> 00:00:46.282
I wanted to bring a fourth
option to my community

00:00:46.282 --> 00:00:48.809
and that's rock climbing.

00:00:48.809 --> 00:00:50.740
I co-founded Brothers of Climbing,

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:53.860
an organization formed to
tackle the lack of diversity

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:56.849
in rock climbing and to help promote

00:00:56.849 --> 00:01:00.074
and encourage people of color
and underrepresented groups

00:01:00.074 --> 00:01:02.436
to get in the outdoors.

00:01:02.436 --> 00:01:04.735
It's for men, women, anyone.

00:01:04.735 --> 00:01:06.687
If you feel underrepresented in climbing,

00:01:06.687 --> 00:01:08.756
you belong with us.

00:01:08.756 --> 00:01:10.655
When the group formed,
there were only three of us,

00:01:10.655 --> 00:01:14.233
and now there's dozens of us,
and that's a great feeling.

00:01:14.233 --> 00:01:16.716
In New York City we
host a monthly meet up.

00:01:16.716 --> 00:01:19.172
Across the country we
wanna host a festival

00:01:19.172 --> 00:01:22.755
and then just other
events in other cities.

00:01:24.988 --> 00:01:28.068
There are many reasons why
there's a lack of representation

00:01:28.068 --> 00:01:30.021
in the sport of rock climbing.

00:01:30.021 --> 00:01:32.430
One reason is there's not too many mentors

00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:37.137
within our community teaching
and spreading the knowledge.

00:01:37.137 --> 00:01:39.380
When I grew up, I never had that.

00:01:39.380 --> 00:01:41.737
Also, the industry doesn't do a great job

00:01:41.737 --> 00:01:44.459
showing the diversity
that is in the sport.

00:01:44.459 --> 00:01:46.993
You can open up a catalog
and you won't find

00:01:46.993 --> 00:01:48.716
a person of color in it.

00:01:48.716 --> 00:01:50.785
You know, the minute you get out
there and you start doing it

00:01:50.785 --> 00:01:53.923
and you realize how easy
it is, something clicks

00:01:53.923 --> 00:01:55.855
and then you say, "I can do this.

00:01:55.855 --> 00:01:56.913
"I can do this, I'm doing it."

00:01:56.913 --> 00:02:00.921
I'm doing it and I want
other people to realize that.

00:02:00.921 --> 00:02:04.171
(mellow chiming music)

00:02:05.823 --> 00:02:08.406
(bell chiming)

